          "Now, turn to the moment the two preceding concepts, Ostpolitik and Wirtschaftsdiplomatie, were both tested at once. Chancellor Olaf Scholz's declaration of a Zeitenwende, a turning point or epochal shift, delivered to the Bundestag just three days after Russia's February 2022 invasion of Ukraine, marked a rapid, historically unusual policy shift: a commitment to a special one-hundred-billion-euro defense fund, a pledge to meet NATO's 2% of GDP defense-spending target on an ongoing basis, and a break from decades of German restraint on exporting weapons into active conflict zones. The mechanism behind the speed of this shift was less a change in underlying German values than a sudden collapse of the empirical assumption Wandel durch Handel rested on, that a state as economically enmeshed with Germany as Russia would not risk a full-scale war, an assumption Russia's actual behavior disproved within days and that left the political consensus behind decades of restraint with remarkably little to defend itself on. The limit of the Zeitenwende, visible from its earliest months onward, is that declaring a turning point rhetorically proved far easier than actually executing one institutionally, since defense procurement, personnel recruitment, and industrial capacity all move on multi-year timelines a single speech cannot compress.",
