        example:
          "Significant tax reforms have gone through extended Vermittlungsausschuss negotiations spanning weeks, with the eventual compromise text differing meaningfully from either chamber's original position, the formal mediation process itself shaping, not just rubber-stamping, the final outcome. The 2023 Bürgergeld reform covered in this course's German Domestic Policy lecture moved through exactly this process, with the CDU/CSU-controlled Bundesrat using its Zustimmungsgesetz leverage to force Vermittlungsausschuss negotiation that tightened the bill's original sanction rules before finally granting consent. The 2019 Grundsteuerreform likewise required extended Vermittlungsausschuss-adjacent negotiation over how much local variation individual Länder would retain in setting their own property-tax rates, and the eventual compromise preserved a broader Länder opt-out than the original federal draft had proposed, itself a direct, traceable product of the mediation process.",
